cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Syllabus Studio, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Syllabus Studio"
abstract: >-
  Syllabus Studio is a browser-based platform for developing academic syllabi
  consistently across a program while preserving instructor control over
  course-specific content. A program director maintains one course catalog,
  designates each syllabus field as locked or instructor-editable, and publishes
  a link-based tool to each instructor; the instructor supplies term-specific
  content and exports a finished syllabus as PDF, Microsoft Word, or
  inline-styled HTML for a learning management system. Institutional content is
  resolved from the catalog at render time, so policy revisions propagate to
  completed syllabi without displacing instructor-authored work. Course
  calendars are generated from institutional term rules for semester or quarter
  systems and support in-person, hybrid, and online asynchronous delivery. All
  authoring and document generation occur in the browser; instructor drafts
  remain on the user's device. The platform requires no user accounts, no
  database, and no cloud-hosted data, and deploys to ordinary web hosting.
type: software
